===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{m|gem-pro|*fērō}}. Cognate with Old Saxon ''[[var|vār]]'' ‘ambush’ (Dutch ''[[gevaar]]'' ‘danger’), Old High German ''[[fara|fāra]]'' ‘ambush, danger, deceit’ (German ''[[Gefahr]]'' ‘danger’).

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|/fæːr/|lang=ang}}

====Noun====
{{ang-noun|m|head=fǣr}}

# sudden [[danger]], [[calamity]], [[ambush]]; a [[blitz]]

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ang|færgripe|fǣrgripe}}
* {{l|ang|færgryre|fǣrgryre}}

=====Descendants=====
* English: [[fear]]

===Etymology 2===
From the same Germanic source as {{m|ang|faran}}. Cognate with Old High German ''[[fuora]]'' (German {{m|de|Fuhre}}).

====Pronunciation====
